      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm assuming you mean gestures that detect thumb location such as thumbs up. If that's the case, that's not really a vrc thing. Not sure about the Quest, but the Rift and Rift S have capacitive (or maybe proximity) sensors in the thumbsticks and ab/xy buttons to tell when your finger is resting on the buttons. That's how Oculus achieves \"finger tracking\". Afaik, there's not much vrchat can do about that as it's a hardware implementation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-16T18:37:48.597Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would like to request that, for VR users, thumb-altering hand poses get linked to something other than the thumbstick, possibly one of the other thumb buttons.\nThis is an especially noticeable problem on the Oculus Quest (I'm not sure about the other VR implementations), where the thumbsticks have an amazing degree of sensitivity, causing the thumb to tuck in, not on a click, but with the slightest pressure, such as having your thumb on the thumbstick at all, basically.\nIf this is somehow a problem, a possible solution is to maybe have the hands remain in whatever state the user sets them to, until detoggled, possibly either by repeating the motion, to turn it off, as a simple detoggle, or by changing the hand position by entering in a new hand pose command.",
